  "body": "## Summary\n\nPR2770 bounds an initialized evaluator and PR2778 bounds isolated form constructors. This adds the complete closed adapter-coefficient lifetime for unchanged PR2697, above **all** numerical entry residents:\n\n```text\nselected_coefficient, adapter branch\n  Callback initialization and validation\n  current projector preparation\n  good/fallback form construction\n  Page.evaluate\n  close form, columns and callback\n\nadditional residue Words <= 37,672\nadditional index Words   <= 22\n```\n\nA complete rank-42 call attains the residue bound. Only `research/selected-adapter-numerical-lifecycle/` is added, with a written lifetime proof, six byte-identical source modules and their complete notice, exact pins, an independent integer fixture oracle, fixed receipt and registered replay.\n\n[Canonical claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2319#discussioncomment-18959295). Scope changes from the historical helper-contract suggestion to the live selected numerical-overlap handoff. Credit Jose Manuel/jmbarrancoml's PR2697 algorithms; Nick Petalas's PR2759/2770/2778 components; David Arias's PR2753 coarser logical inventory and the retained source lineage. Exact heads and attribution are in TASK.json and SNAPSHOT.json.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** An initialized-Page allowance does not include its simultaneously retained projector and constructor matrices. **After:** The closed entry point fits the source-derived 37,672/22 allowance; a literal F3 rank-42 call attains 37,672. Nested fallback evaluation separately reaches 36,877.\n- **Before:** Fixture teardown could conceal source leaks or an insufficient construction allowance. **After:** Twelve optimized controls check actual source rollback before teardown, including a one-Word-underbudget constructor, post-construction nested evaluation failure, index exhaustion and wrong Page binding. Scalar, borrowed-state, source-integrity and typed-receipt checks pass.\n- Registered CPython 3.12.15 replay passes eight complete 64-dimensional fixtures and 202 occupied-cell scans. A Git-free export passes both commands without changing file hashes. Scoped Ruff, package pins/metadata, local links and 74 workflow tests pass, with seven workflow skips. Separate internal source/proof/checker review and replay pass; no independent human review is claimed.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -Werror -B \\\n  scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-adapter-numerical-lifecycle\n```\n\nSubmission refresh checked canonical main `6ca6f217708b075814de409ad693fea9a2aaa760`, unchanged guidance/selection/runner and all dependency heads. Complete metadata pagination covered 717 open PRs and 1,423 Discussion records without warnings; searches exclude arbitrary code diffs.\n\nThe bound concerns successful numerical content under the pinned source contracts. Finite fixtures do not establish selected-catalogue membership or exhaust cross adapters, nonzero coordinates and nonuniform ancestor weights. The child branch, surrounding caller residents, serialized tapes, backing capacity, physical placement/movement and full reserve admission remain separate. No selected cold replay, formal-kernel result, hosted-CI pass, new supplier or kappa claim.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way\n\nOne additive research package; frozen sources and selected-frontier files are unchanged.\n\n**Blast Radius:** Research\n\nThe opt-in replay adds bounded CI work. Applying its allowance to a whole caller still requires an explicit entry-resident and physical-cost ledger.\n",
